# Paul's own apps: built in their own private repos, published as GitHub
# releases, installed and kept current by `dots apps` (run by every
# `dots sync` and by install.sh). Never put a build in this repo: it is public,
# and a bundle can carry things like an OAuth client.
#
# One app per line, whitespace-separated:
#
#   name  kind     repo                asset          id               restart
#
# kind     flatpak: the release asset is a Flatpak bundle, installed --user.
#          bundle: the asset is a .tar.gz of directories, each of which
#          replaces ~/.local/share/<dir>, plus bin/, copied to ~/.local/bin.
# id       flatpak: the Flatpak application id. bundle: the command in bin/,
#          which is also the process name. Used to find what is installed and
#          whether the running copy is older than it.
# restart  the rest of the line: the command that restarts the app onto a new
#          build. Printed, never run — killing a mail client mid-session is
#          your call, not dots'.
#
# Adding an app is one line here, plus its repo on the read-only token (see
# README, "Your own apps").

relay  flatpak  paulhmurray/relay  relay.flatpak  app.relay.Relay  flatpak kill app.relay.Relay && mail
cadence  bundle   paulhmurray/cadence  cadence.tar.gz  cadence          pkill -x cadence; sleep 1; music ensure
